  "detail": "The operator\u2019s November3 amendment explicitly permits only full-unit-stage hang guards to rise120s to240s if the cleaned-host full suite exceeds120s, keeping actual timings. The nine commands already ran first under120s in385. The same unchanged two-worker Vitest workload now takes128.35s in429 on the cleaned host (129.079s command), so the condition is met. Change only the name===unit ternary in the nine contract runners. Unit commands still run the entire suite with maxWorkers2, which matches the current default. Every other timeout, per-case deadline, heartbeat, cancellation/kill policy, assertion, fault control and timing collector remains exact.",
  "validation": "Each of the nine files is byte-identical to its predecessor after the single inverse240000\u2192120000 unit-branch replacement. The existing62 wrapper/fixture controls pass without edits, as do quality/format,17registry checks, inventory and10controls. The449-source runtime/crypto census and all constructions remain identical. Inventory changes only nine script fingerprints and the same nine derived unit-guard clauses; every other field/count/case/obligation is unchanged (732files/726required). Two private review assumptions initially fail: the commands use literal Vitest paths with explicit maxWorkers2 rather than resolve(), and inventory campaign data legitimately embeds those guard clauses. Preserve both failures, verify the actual command/default, and compare the entire inventory after normalizing exactly those nine authorized clauses. No app or old-test change. This is not a new full-unit result or claim that all nine campaigns have already run under240s; the forthcoming coherent checkpoint will retain each actual unit duration.",
  "summary": "The nine full-suite stages now use the already approved240s hang guard. Exact inverse source review and all62 existing wrapper controls pass; per-case/native/performance deadlines and runtime source remain unchanged.",
  "limitations": "Guard-only harness maintenance under an existing conditional operator approval, not a new gate relaxation or performance result. Full campaign execution, coherent Stage3/4 checkpoint and Stage5/6 remain. No crypto/format/trust/budget/limit/sender/default change, new lab, commit, publication or deployment. The latest full unit remains429\u2019s330files/3,210pass/one skip128.35s.",
  "decisionTitle": "Exercise the existing conditional full-unit timeout approval and retain actual suite times",
  "decision": "Use the measured cleaned-host full-suite duration and identical two-worker command to invoke the operator\u2019s existing240s hang-guard approval. Limit the change to the full-suite unit branch, preserve every other source byte, and keep unit-timing.json reporting elapsed/deadline/code/timeout on each campaign. Do not change any individual test or frozen16ms/2.5s/30s/600s/15s/120s predicate.",
  "next": "Close the Stage3/4 evidence map and run the full coherent functional checkpoint with display protection,5s host/fseventsd/swap logs and actual unit times. Then execute the declared Stage5 cells/report-only work and Stage6; continue automatically after each freeze.",
